A2ZYNQ - Licensing
==================

A2ZYNQ is a port of the A2FPGA Multicard core (https://github.com/a2fpga/a2fpga_core)
to the Smart Zynq SP board. Most of the logic in hdl/ and boards/ came from
A2FPGA, and I kept its licensing exactly as it is upstream. Like A2FPGA, the
licensing here is layered: the license header in each file is authoritative
for that file, and this document explains how the pieces fit together.

1. Code from A2FPGA, and code I wrote for A2ZYNQ
------------------------------------------------

Files from the A2FPGA project that do not state a different license in their
header are under the MIT License (full text below), copyright the A2FPGA
contributors.

The files I wrote or changed for A2ZYNQ (the Smart Zynq wrapper in
boards/a2n20v2-SmartZynq/rtl, the build scripts, a2hostd changes, the disk
menu, the SSC network bridge, the tests and the tools) are released under the
same MIT License, copyright Ricardo Cervantes, unless their header says
otherwise.

2. Third-party code
-------------------

Files from other authors keep their original licenses, as stated in their
headers. Most are permissive (MIT/BSD-style). These components are under the
GNU General Public License (full texts in the LICENSES/ directory):

  - hdl/support/via6522.vhd - VIA 6522 core, Gideon Zweijtzer
    (1541ultimate project), GPL-3.0
  - hdl/support/TMS5220.vhd - TMS5220 speech chip core, d18c7db,
    GPL-3.0-or-later
  - hdl/support/iir_filter.v (and board-local copies) - audio IIR filter,
    Sorgelig (MiSTer project), GPL-2.0-or-later
  - hdl/disk/hdd_rom.a65 - ProDOS HDD controller firmware, adapted from
    AppleWin, GPL-2.0-or-later
  - boards/a2n20v2-SmartZynq/src/a2hostd/src/gcr_dsk.c - 6-and-2 GCR codec
    ported from AppleWin, GPL-2.0-or-later

3. Combined works
-----------------

The complete logic design for the board includes GPL components listed
above, so the A2ZYNQ bitstream is a combined work conveyed, as a whole, under
the GNU General Public License version 3 (LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt). The same goes
for the a2hostd binary, which links the AppleWin-derived GCR codec. The
corresponding source is this repository, including the scripts needed to
rebuild the bitstream and a2hostd.

The MIT license on the A2FPGA and A2ZYNQ files is GPL-compatible: you can
still take those individual files into other projects under MIT terms. If you
build a design from this repository that includes any of the GPL components,
your combined design is subject to the GPL.

4. Things that are NOT in this repository
-----------------------------------------

The Xillinux evaluation kit for the Smart Zynq SP (block design, boot files,
Linux image) belongs to Xillybus Ltd. and is distributed by them under their
own terms. The build downloads nothing and redistributes nothing from it; you
get it yourself (see third_party/README.md). Vivado and its IP cores are
AMD/Xilinx products under AMD's license.

Apple II disk images, ROMs and software (Total Replay, games, ProDOS, DOS 3.3,
IP65) are not included. Total Replay and IP65 are free downloads from their
own projects.

The proto card schematics and wiring notes in hardware/ are my own work and
are not derived from the GPL components above.

If you reuse any code from this project, check the header of each file you
take to confirm that your intended use is covered.

